    "body": "**Physical iPhone Safari follow-up, PR #431 exact HEAD `12f3bfab2a32b8440f60fe1b4d4d4da3427de91e` (31 Oct 2026): PARTIAL ACCEPTANCE, 3 outstanding UX points.**\n\nThe owner attached 3 real-device screenshots in ChatGPT showing the same DM tab at different moments. These images are currently in the owner's chat, not GitHub attachments; do not claim they are included in this issue comment.\n\n1. **DM panel size changes after initial render.** When the page/tab first loads, DM is compact and general chat receives space. A short time later, with no deliberate resize, the lower DM panel expands substantially and general chat loses vertical space. Reproduce with delayed timers/state changes and both empty and populated DM; log transitions for `--mobile-chat-height`, `--mobile-panels-height`, activeTab, dmPriority, count, active focus, visualViewport and actual DOM rects. Confirm the actual trigger (render/count observer/resize/initialization) before changing code. For zero usable DM conversations keep compact mode stable; do not shrink populated DM with active messages or composer.\n2. **Owner-proposed mobile interaction:** tapping the *already selected* `Личка` / `Баттлы` / `События` tab again should collapse/expand the *whole lower tab panel*, allowing general chat to expand into available viewport. A tap on a different tab selects and expands that tab. Preserve keyboard focus and restore manual resize preference; accessible state/ARIA and no breaking swipe, long-press, tab navigation or populated DM. This is a new requested behavior, not previously implemented PASS.\n3. **Asymmetric DM conversation chips:** screenshots show inconsistent pill widths/heights, close-button boxes, clipping and uneven baseline. Normalize chip rows `#dmTabs` / `.dmTab` / `.dmTabLabel` / `.dmTabClose` with consistent alignment, radius, padding, truncated long nick and accessible tap targets. Do not change DM identity/state or core mechanics.\n\n**Scope / gate:** only PR #431 shared mobile shell/UI files and explicitly owned Web/docs mirrors. Do not edit Chat04.1B messaging server or UI-preview PR #453. Check current HEAD, locks and ownership before any new writing. Independent browser tests need delayed post-load state transitions, real hit testing on compact/mobile viewport and empty/nonempty panels, native iPhone Safari owner retest afterward. No merge or deploy permitted by this comment. \n\n**Current owner assessment:** all other previously checked mobile behaviors accepted; PR remains Draft until these UX issues and Safari retest are addressed.",
