    "body": "## Summary\n\n- The mobile profile/statistics header compacts while a chat, DM, or report field is focused and while the keyboard is open; the Menu button stays accessible and the normal header returns after blur.\n- The DM tab shows a clear empty state when there are no conversations, without fake messages. With conversations, the message log gets the main panel space and scrolls independently of the compact conversation list.\n- The report suggestion popup clears the generic public-chat `bottom` anchor that stretched it across unrelated content. Ordinary DM and report flows are tested on separate screens.\n\n## Scope\n\nEight paths differ from the PR base:\n\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-core.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-core.js`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/style-base.css`\n- `docs/style-base.css`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-dm.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-dm.js`\n- `tools/test_mobile_shell_regressions.html`\n- `tools/test_mobile_shell_user_scroll.mjs`\n\nAll three Web/docs pairs are byte-identical.\n\n## Verification on exact HEAD `af016d7ee57285ef3c87c1a2285b305354598c7a`\n\n- Headless Chromium full runner: **187/187 PASS** across 320×568, 360×640, 390×844, 430×932, 768×1024, 1280×720 and 1440×900.\n- **10 fixture-only SKIP**, explicitly excluded from PASS: unavailable battle action entry and saved panel-scroll restoration in five mobile/tablet fixtures.\n- At 320×568, trusted wheel checks cover ordinary DM thread-list scrolling, independent old-message history scrolling, composer hit target, separate report-list screen, popup anchoring and scroll, last-option selection, retained input focus, and submit-button hit testing.\n- Empty DM, multiple conversations, header compact/restore behavior, tab switching, history priority, and report list accessibility are included in the regression runner.\n- `python3 tools/test_mobile_first_interface_contract.py`: **14/14 PASS**.\n- Node syntax checks, `git diff --check`, and all three mirror comparisons: PASS.\n- GitHub Actions [ai-forensics-evidence #41142559516](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/41142559516): **SUCCESS**.\n- Independent read-only review of this exact HEAD: **no blocking defect found**.\n\nPhysical iPhone Safari and its native keyboard still require owner verification. This PR remains Draft; no device acceptance or merge approval is claimed.",
